  VERDICT (write): ENDPOINT BOUND -- concentrated writers reached 42% of the
  scaling the same writers reached fanned out.

  SUSTAINED WRITE vs READ at the SAME endpoint, 64 participants:
    read  22.090 B/cycle
    write 21.264 B/cycle   ratio 0.963
    -> the endpoint sustains writes and reads at the same rate to within
       5%. A rate campaign cannot then distinguish the two directions'
       OCCUPANCY, whatever their latencies differ by.
    This is an OCCUPANCY comparison and not a latency one. It cannot price a
    single write, cannot split service time from queueing, and -- with the
    samecore arm absent on this part -- cannot tell the endpoint from the one
    inbound router link every concentrated flow converges on. Report "the
    endpoint", never "the channel". CORROBORATION, never provenance.
